---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import Message from "../../components/Message.astro"
import StreamPreview from "../../components/StreamPreview.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Overview · Threa Developers"
  description="The Threa public REST API: what it covers, the base URL, and a quickstart that goes from creating an API key to your first memo search."
  current="overview"
>
  <h1>Your workspace, over HTTP.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Messages, streams, members, attachments, and the memos Threa builds from
    your conversations. Your own agent reads the same memory Ariadne does.
  </p>

  <StreamPreview stream="platform">
    <Message author="maya" time="14:02">
      <div class="tl-text"><span class="mention">@my-agent</span> why did we pause the auth refactor?</div>
    </Message>
    <Message author="my-agent" time="14:02">
      <div class="tl-text">It's on hold until Jordan's review of the token-rotation model.</div>
      <div class="recall-memo-card">
        <div class="rmc-icon"><svg><use href="#icon-compass" /></svg></div>
        <div class="rmc-body">
          <div class="rmc-kicker"><span class="k-type">decision</span><span class="k-tag">#product</span></div>
          <div class="rmc-title">Auth refactor held pending token-rotation review</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rmc-meta">Mar 12</div>
      </div>
    </Message>
  </StreamPreview>

  <h2>Quickstart</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Create an API key</h3>
      <p>
        In the app, open <strong>Workspace Settings → API Keys</strong>, create a
        user key, pick the scopes you need, and copy it once. Full walkthrough in
        <a class="link" href="/developers/authentication">Authentication</a>.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Add it to Credentials</h3>
      <p>
        Open <strong>Credentials</strong> (top right) and enter your workspace ID
        and key. Every sample on these pages then uses your values, and
        <strong>Run</strong> calls the API. They stay in your browser and go out
        only on requests you run.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Confirm who you are</h3>
      <p><code>GET /me</code> needs no scope and returns the identity behind the key.</p>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        label="Who am I"
        code={`curl {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/me \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}"`}
        run={{ method: "GET", path: "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/me" }}
      />
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Search what Threa remembers</h3>
      <p>
        With <code>memos:read</code>, search memos the way Ariadne does. Results
        link back to their source messages.
      </p>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        label="Search memos"
        code={`curl -X POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/memos/search \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{ "query": "auth", "limit": 5 }'`}
        run={{
          method: "POST",
          path: "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/memos/search",
          body: `{ "query": "auth", "limit": 5 }`,
        }}
      />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Base URL</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>API</dt>
    <dd><code>https://app.threa.io/api/v1</code></dd>
    <dt>Workspace routes</dt>
    <dd><code>/workspaces/&#123;workspaceId&#125;/…</code></dd>
    <dt>Workspace ID</dt>
    <dd>In the app URL, after <code>/w/</code></dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>Working with an AI agent</h2>
  <p>
    Every page has a markdown mirror at its URL plus <code>.md</code>.
    <a class="link" href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a> is the whole set in
    one fetch, and the <a class="link" href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI spec</a> is
    the contract. Hand your agent this:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="text"
    label="Prompt for your agent"
    code={`Integrate with the Threa API. Read https://threa.io/llms-full.txt for the docs
and https://threa.io/openapi.json for the exact contract. The base URL is
{{baseUrl}}, my workspace ID is {{workspaceId}}, and my API key is in the
THREA_API_KEY environment variable (send it as "Authorization: Bearer ...").
Verify the key with GET /api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/me before anything else.`}
  />
  <p>
    Keep the key in an environment variable, not in the prompt. Agents that
    speak MCP can use <code>threa mcp serve</code> instead; see
    <a class="link" href="/developers/cli">CLI &amp; MCP server</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can build</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Post and read messages</strong> in any stream you can access, with idempotent sends.</li>
    <li><strong>Search</strong> messages and memos, semantic or exact, by stream, type, and date.</li>
    <li><strong>Pull memos with their sources</strong>, so your agent works from what Ariadne knows.</li>
    <li><strong>Run your own agent as a bot</strong> that answers when it's mentioned. See <a class="link" href="/developers/recipes#local-agent">the recipe</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Upload attachments</strong> and read the text Threa extracts from them.</li>
    <li><strong>Take alerts</strong> from tools you already run, over an <a class="link" href="/developers/incoming-webhooks">incoming webhook</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
